 "hints": [
  {
   "id": "HINT-01",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Which operation do you expect to happen more frequently: creating a short URL or redirecting a visitor?"
  },
  {
   "id": "HINT-02",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Think about the creation path and redirect path separately. They perform different operations and may have different traffic patterns."
  },
  {
   "id": "HINT-03",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "The redirect path repeatedly looks up mappings by short code. Which storage access pattern would make that lookup efficient?"
  },
  {
   "id": "HINT-04",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "If many requests resolve the same popular short codes, consider whether a cache could reduce repeated database reads."
  },
  {
   "id": "HINT-05",
   "level": 5,
   "text": "A possible redirect flow is: client request, application resolver, cache lookup, database lookup on cache miss, and redirect response. Consider what happens when the cache is unavailable."
  }
 ]
